# timeline (G4 §3.3 macro) — a clock's coordinates in order, each with its members. A coordinate is a
# Set, so this is the generic ordered rendering: `clock=world:default` is the shared world's history
# (env + sync records, plus the tick-only coordinates the old world.axis dropped); `clock=wb:<bench>`
# is a bench's execution + thought record in the order it happened; `clock=wf:<bench>:<branch>` is the
# plan in order. Coarser than the Set primitives, so it is a MACRO — never a kernel handler. This
# replaces world.axis (kept one release as an alias that runs this macro).
#
#!params clock=world:default,from=1,to=
cronon.timeline clock="$clock" from="$from" to="$to"
